nto the tree, causing 5 more apples to fall out. He picked up these apples and put all but one in his pocket. He threw the remaining apple into the tree, causing 6 more apples to fall out. He picked up all the remaining apples and went home. He had 2 + 5 + 6 = 13 apples. The answer is 13.\n\nAnswer_23:\nAli orders 850 kilos of coal. The coal is delivered in 50 kg bags, so he orders 850 / 50 = 17 bags. Each bag costs $18, so the total cost is 17 * 18 = 306 dollars. The answer is 306.\n\nAnswer_24:\nKate's friends eat 6 cheese pizza slices and 4 pepperoni pizza slices each. There are 6 friends, so they eat 6 * 6 = 36 cheese pizza slices and 6 * 4 = 24 pepperoni pizza slices. Since each pizza has 12 slices, Kate needs to buy 36 / 12 = 3 cheese pizzas and 24 / 8 = 3 pepperoni pizzas. The answer is 6.\n\nAnswer_25:\nSam runs 3 miles on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday. He runs 5 miles on Tuesday and Thursday. The total number of miles he runs is 3 * 3 + 5 * 2 = 9 + 10 = 19 miles. The answer is 19.\n\nAnswer_26:\nJay can build 20 snowballs per hour. He can build 20 / 15 = 1.33 snowballs per 15 minutes. He wants to build 60 snowballs, so it will take him 60 / 1.33 = 45 hours. The answer is 45.\n\nAnswer_27:\nJohn is 28 years old now. When Digimon came out, John was twice as old as Jim. Let's denote Jim's age at that time as x. John's age at that time was 2x. The difference between their ages is 28 - 2x = x. Simplifying, we get 28 = 3x. Dividing both sides by 3, we get x = 28 / 3 = 9.33. Since Jim's age is not a fraction, we round down to 9. The answer is 9.\n\nAnswer_28:\nDoxa eats 1 slice of apple. Her sister eats 1 more slice than Doxa, so she eats 2 slices. Her brother eats 1 more slice than her sister, so he eats 3 slices. The total number of slices eaten is 1 + 2 + 3 = 6. The answer is 6.\n\nAnswer_29:\nThe nurses used 38 bandages on the first day and ordered 1 pack of 50 bandages. They used 38 - 10 = 28 bandages on the second day and ordered 2 packs of 50 bandages. They