is 600 + 1440 = 2040 dollars. The answer is 2040.\n\nAnswer_37:\nMr. Julius plants 20 White Oak trees on the first day. He plants twice as many Lodgepole Pine trees, so he plants 2 * 20 = 40 Lodgepole Pine trees. On the second day, he plants 10 more White Oak trees, so he plants 20 + 10 = 30 White Oak trees. He plants 1/4 more Lodgepole Pine trees than on the first day, so he plants 1/4 * 40 = 10 Lodgepole Pine trees. The total number of trees planted is 20 + 40 + 30 + 10 = 100 trees. The answer is 100.\n\nAnswer_38:\nFred made 24 gallons of root beer on the first day. His children drank 4 gallons, so he had 24 - 4 = 20 gallons left. His wife spilled 7 gallons, so he had 20 - 7 = 13 gallons left. His friend Ronnie drank 5 gallons, so he had 13 - 5 = 8 gallons left. He shared the remaining root beer equally among 3 people, so each person got 8 / 3 = 2.67 gallons. The answer is 2.67.",
